IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-types`
IMPORT `eia-dates`

-- Electricity Industry Act 2010 — GOAL 1: THE SUPPLY OBLIGATION.
--
--   "Must the distributor keep supplying the place; is the obligation ended
--    or suspended; has it committed the offence; and when may it switch the
--    place to an alternative source?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2010_116.txt — ss 105-107.

§ `Goal 1 — the supply obligation`

-- s 105 "(2) A distributor to whom this section applies must, in relation to
-- the place ..., either— (a) supply line function services to the place ...;
-- or (b) supply the place with electricity from an alternative source. (3) The
-- obligation ... is subject to anything to the contrary in the Electricity Act
-- 1992, any regulations ..., or any written agreement, entered into before
-- this section comes into force". s 106 "(1) A distributor's obligation ...
-- comes to an end with respect to a place if— (a) the landowner and (if the
-- landowner is not the consumer) the consumer, or the Minister, agree in
-- writing ...; or (b) the obligation is assigned to, or assumed by, a
-- successor in business".
@ref ss 105(1)-(3), 106(1)
GIVEN s IS A `Supply facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply obligation continues` s IF
        s's `section 105 applies to the distributor and place`
    AND NOT s's `a contrary agreement or enactment under s 105(3)`
    AND NOT s's `ending agreed in writing by the landowner, consumer or Minister`
    AND NOT s's `assigned to or assumed by a successor`

-- s 106 "(2) The obligation ... is suspended ... in any of the following
-- circumstances: (a) the supply ... has ceased as a result of circumstances
-- beyond the control of the distributor ...: (b) the supply ... needs to cease
-- for reasons of safety or in order to carry out maintenance or upgrading
-- work: (c) the distributor, or a retailer, is entitled to cease supply ...
-- because of a failure to pay money due ... (3) If the supply ... ceases in
-- any of the circumstances described in subsection (2), the cessation may
-- continue only for as long as the reason for cessation continues."
@ref s 106(2)-(3)
GIVEN s IS A `Supply facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply obligation is suspended` s IF
        NOT s's `reason supply ceased` EQUALS `supply has not ceased`
    AND NOT s's `reason supply ceased` EQUALS `another reason`
    AND s's `the reason for ceasing still continues`

-- s 105 "(4) A distributor who is obliged under subsection (2) ... commits an
-- offence, and is liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 and to
-- a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- which the offence continues, if the distributor,— (a) having been made
-- aware that supply to the place has ceased in the circumstances described in
-- section 106(2)(a), fails to resume supply as soon as is reasonable in the
-- circumstances; or (b) knowingly ceases to supply ... other than in the
-- circumstances described in section 106(2)(b) or (c)."
@ref ss 105(4), 106(2)
@export Whether a distributor commits the s 105(4) offence under the Electricity Industry Act 2010 (NZ) while its supply obligation continues: failing to resume as soon as reasonable after supply stopped for reasons beyond its control, or knowingly ceasing supply other than for safety, maintenance or upgrading, or non-payment (or after the reason has passed). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Supply facts`  @desc Whether s 105 applies, any contrary agreement, ending or assignment, why supply ceased and whether the reason continues, and the distributor's response
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` s IF
        `the supply obligation continues` s
    AND CONSIDER s's `reason supply ceased`
        WHEN `supply has not ceased` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control` THEN NOT s's `resumed as soon as reasonable after learning of it`
        WHEN `(b) safety, maintenance or upgrading` THEN s's `ceased knowingly` AND NOT s's `the reason for ceasing still continues`
        WHEN `(c) non-payment of money due for the place` THEN s's `ceased knowingly` AND NOT s's `the reason for ceasing still continues`
        WHEN `another reason` THEN s's `ceased knowingly`

@ref s 105(4)
GIVEN continuing IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most fine for the s 105(4) offence, days continuing` continuing MEANS
    10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES continuing

-- s 107 "(1) A distributor ... who proposes to comply with section 105(2) by
-- supplying a place with electricity from an alternative source, must give
-- at least 6 months' notice of the proposal". The 6 months run from the day
-- after the notice and end under the Legislation Act 2019 ss 54, 56; the
-- alternative supply may begin the next day (fork F1; changed after the
-- independent pass).
@ref s 107(1); Legislation Act 2019 ss 54, 56
GIVEN notice IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` notice MEANS
    `the day` 1 `days after` (`the last day of a period of` 6 `months beginning with` (`the day` 1 `days after` notice))
